{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.QBetaEnergyDictionary","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.QBetaEnergyDictionary","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Thermo.partition_sum_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Thermo.partition_sum_eq","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/QBetaEnergyDictionary.lean#L75-L82","doc":"**Partition function = Frobenius sum**: summing the Boltzmann weights\nof the read-off energies over the Wedderburn blocks (with degeneracies\n`d`) recovers the Frobenius weighted sum `∑ d_λ y_λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Thermo.energyOf_le_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Thermo.energyOf_le_iff","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/QBetaEnergyDictionary.lean#L67-L73","doc":"**Order-reversing**: at positive inverse temperature, a larger\nFrobenius weight is a *lower* energy — the dominant Wedderburn block is\nthe ground state. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Thermo.energyOf_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Thermo.energyOf_unique","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/QBetaEnergyDictionary.lean#L56-L65","doc":"**Uniqueness**: any energy whose Boltzmann weight is `y` equals the\nread-off energy (the Boltzmann map is injective). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Thermo.boltzmann_energyOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Thermo.boltzmann_energyOf","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/QBetaEnergyDictionary.lean#L48-L54","doc":"**Read-off is correct**: the energy `E_λ = -ln y/β` reproduces the\nBoltzmann weight `y` (for `β ≠ 0`, `y > 0`). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:beta-eq-ln-q-dictionary","label":"prop:beta-eq-ln-q-dictionary","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/beta-eq-ln-q-dictionary.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Thermo.logPos_of_one_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Thermo.logPos_of_one_lt","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/QBetaEnergyDictionary.lean#L43-L46","doc":"For the substrate regime `q > 1`, the inverse temperature `β = ln q`\nis positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Thermo.energyOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Thermo.energyOf","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/QBetaEnergyDictionary.lean#L40-L41","doc":"Energy read off from a positive weight: `E = -ln y / β`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Thermo.boltzmann","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Thermo.boltzmann","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/QBetaEnergyDictionary.lean#L37-L38","doc":"Boltzmann weight `e^{-β E}` at inverse temperature `β`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}